    "https://employment.niu.edu/postings/97604": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Epistemology (6584)",
      "description": "Northern Illinois University | Assistant Professor - Epistemology (6584) Skip to Main Content Find your Career at Northern Illinois University! Toggle navigation Home Search All Jobs Log In /Create Account Help NIU Human Resources Assistant Professor - Epistemology (6584) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Working Position Title Assistant Professor - Epistemology (6584) Classification Title Assistant Professor Position Number 00006584 Posting Date 10/05/2026 Closing Date Priority Review Date 11/06/2026 Business Unit Description Faculty Full-Time/Part Time Full-Time FTE 1.00 Position Status Regular FLSA Exempt Job Code 2000 Union Representation Union Union Code UFA - United Faculty Alliance Unit/Department Philosophy College/Unit College of LA&S Dean Division Academic Division Location ZH 915 Link to Department Website or Custom Search Page Department of Philosophy Position Summary, Requirements, and Qualifications Position Summary, Requirements, and Qualifications Overview The Department of Philosophy at Northern Illinois University invites applications for a tenure-track appointment, at the rank of Assistant Professor, to begin August 16, 2027. We seek a candidate who shows promise of excellence in teaching and research in the area of epistemology, with competence in metaphysics, philosophy of AI, ethics, logic, or early modern philosophy. Responsibilities include undergraduate and graduate (master’s level) teaching at the standard load (2/2 for research-active faculty), research, advising, and committee work. Ph.D. required by the start date. Northern Illinois University ( NIU ) is one of the largest public universities in the state of Illinois, with approximately 16,000 students. NIU is a Carnegie Doctoral/Research University-Higher Research Activity institution located in DeKalb, an affordable and growing community 65 miles west of Chicago. We strive to improve outcomes for all students by identifying and removing barriers that disproportionately hinder the academic achievement and student experience of historically and currently underserved populations. The Department of Philosophy is committed to building and sustaining inclusive and equitable working and learning environments for all its students, staff, and faculty. It offers both a baccalaureate program and a terminal master’s program. Position Summary The Assistant Professor of Philosophy will be an active researcher who teaches undergraduate and graduate courses for the Department of Philosophy. Additional responsibilities include committee work and student advising. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate philosophy courses (2/2 for research-active faculty) Publish and engage in related scholarly activities Provide service to the department, university, and profession Mentor students Contribute to exam and departmental committees, as needed Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Philosophy by the start date Specialization in Epistemology Competence in metaphysics, philosophy of AI, ethics, logic, or early modern philosophy Additional Requirements N/A Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated commitment to effective teaching and mentoring a diverse student population Physical Demands Summary For physical demands and requirements please see human resources policies and protocols. Appointment and Compensation Details Appointment and Compensation Details Anticipated Appointment Start Date 08/16/2027 Anticipated Appointment End Date Percent of Staff Year 0.75 Standard Hours Per Week 37.50 Salary Starting at $72,000.00 for 9 months. Faculty compensation is governed by the UFA CBA . NIU offers a robust  benefits package. Hourly or Semi-monthly Pay Rate/Range Starting at $4,000.00 per pay period. Faculty compensation is governed by the UFA CBA. NIU offers a robust benefits package . Earn Type Salary Application Procedure Application Procedure Application Procedure Full consideration will be given to all applications received by November 6, 2026. Applicants should visit Assistant Professor – Epistemology to submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Writing sample Research statement, describing current research and future research plans Teaching portfolio, including a statement of teaching philosophy and experience, a sample syllabus for an upper-level epistemology course, and (if applicable) results of teaching evaluations Transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable for initial review of application) In addition, please arrange to have three letters of recommendation sent on your behalf to philosophy@niu.edu . Applications submitted after November 6, 2026 are welcomed, but will be considered only as needed. Official graduate transcripts are required upon hire. Successful completion of a background check is also required upon hire. Questions can be directed to philosophy department chair, Jason Hanna, jhanna@niu.edu . Special Instructions Quick Link to Applicant https://employment.niu.edu/postings/97589 Is Background Check Required Yes EEO Statement Summary In accordance with applicable statutes and regulations, NIU is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, religion, age, disability (physical and mental), marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender (identity and expression), political affiliation, or any other factor unrelated to professional qualifications, and will comply with all applicable federal and state statutes, regulations and orders pertaining to nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Director of Civil Rights Office, Title IX Coordinator Health Services 2nd floor CivilRights@niu.edu 815-753-0455 Visa Policy In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification document form upon hire. ADA Accommodation NIU remains committed to ensuring that its recruitment and application procedures include full opportunities for applicants with disabilities. Employment opportunities will not be denied to anyone because of the need to make accommodations for a person’s disability during either the application or interview process. An applicant who believes they require an accommodation to participate in the employment process due to a disability may request that accommodation through the Accommodation Request Form . For further assistance, please contact the office of Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity ( AAEO ) at ada@niu.edu . Safety Information NIU provides annual reports on campus security and fire safety. Read the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Contact the Ethics and Compliance Office at 815-753-9364 for a hard copy. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Writing Sample Research Statement Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts (unofficial with official required at hire) Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © 2019 Board of Trustees of Northern Illinois University All rights reserved. Back to Top Northern Illinois University 1425 W. Lincoln Hwy., DeKalb, IL 60115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
