    "https://employment.niu.edu/postings/97880": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Structural Geology (6147)",
      "description": "Northern Illinois University | Assistant Professor in Structural Geology (6147) Skip to Main Content Find your Career at Northern Illinois University! Toggle navigation Home Search All Jobs Log In /Create Account Help NIU Human Resources Assistant Professor in Structural Geology (6147) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Working Position Title Assistant Professor in Structural Geology (6147) Classification Title Assistant Professor Position Number 00006147 Posting Date 10/14/2026 Closing Date Priority Review Date 01/01/2027 Business Unit Description Faculty Full-Time/Part Time Full-Time FTE 1.00 Position Status Regular FLSA Exempt Job Code 2000 Union Representation Union Union Code UFA - United Faculty Alliance Unit/Department Earth Atmosphere & Environment College/Unit College of LA&S Dean Division Academic Division Location DH 312 Link to Department Website or Custom Search Page Department of Earth, Atmosphere and Environment Position Summary, Requirements, and Qualifications Position Summary, Requirements, and Qualifications Overview The Department of Earth, Atmosphere and Environment at Northern Illinois University invites applications for an assistant professor in the field of structural geology or related fields to begin in August 2027. We are seeking an individual whose research interests are in the broad areas of structural geology, tectonics, geophysics/geodynamics, or a closely allied field. The applicant will be expected to develop a teaching and research program that integrates with one or more of the department’s related strengths in experimental mineralogy/petrology, geochemistry, igneous petrology, metamorphic petrology, or mineral physics. The department’s facilities include an array of analytical instruments (e.g., petrographic microscopes, SEM - EDS , XRF , XRD , ion chromatograph, and mass spectrometers) and field equipment. The successful applicant will be expected to establish a vigorous externally funded research program. The successful candidate will contribute to the development of undergraduates in the Department’s B.S. programs, as well as teach, mentor, and advise students at the M.S. and Ph.D. levels. The successful candidate will be expected to teach structural geology and contribute to additional courses that complement their expertise and support departmental curricular needs. Student engagement is a key component to NIU’s mission. As such, the desired candidate will aid in the development of unique learning opportunities that enhance STEM education and outreach. EAE offers programs leading to the B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degrees, and currently has 13 faculty members whose research and teaching interests are described on our department website . NIU is a public research university in DeKalb, an affordable and growing community that is a commutable distance from Chicago and Rockford metropolitan areas. The proximity of DeKalb to Chicago provides easy access to Chicago’s Technology and Research Corridor (Argonne, Fermi, and many Fortune 1000 companies), the arts and extensive nature preserves and parks. Our 16,000+ student body is diverse, with many first-generation and racially and culturally diverse students. NIU is dedicated to fostering an inclusive academic environment where all students, faculty and staff thrive. Position Summary The Assistant Professor will develop and maintain an active teaching and research program in structural geology or a related field. Responsibilities include teaching structural geology and related courses, mentoring and advising undergraduate and graduate students, seeking external research funding, and establishing a vigorous research program that complements departmental strengths. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teach structural geology and related courses supporting the geology-based curriculum Develop and maintain an active research program in structural geology Seek external research funding Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Geology or a related field by the time of appointment Record of or ability to produce publications in respected, peer-reviewed academic journals Evidence of strong research skills and commitment to quality education Ability to teach structural geology Additional Requirements N/A Preferred Qualifications Evidence of high-quality teaching and a plan for experiential learning with diverse students at the undergraduate and/or graduate level Evidence of commitment to service to the science community at a commensurate level with rank Physical Demands Summary For physical demands and requirements please see human resources policies and protocols. Appointment and Compensation Details Appointment and Compensation Details Anticipated Appointment Start Date 8/16/2027 Anticipated Appointment End Date Percent of Staff Year 0.75 Standard Hours Per Week 37.50 Salary Starting at $88,000. Faculty compensation is governed by the UFA CBA . NIU offers a robust benefits package. Hourly or Semi-monthly Pay Rate/Range Starting at $4,888.89 per pay period. Faculty compensation is governed by the UFA CBA. NIU offers a robust benefits package . Earn Type Salary Application Procedure Application Procedure Application Procedure For full consideration, prospective applicants should visit Assistant Professor in Structural Geology to create an application profile and submit the following materials by January 1, 2027 : Letter of interest Curriculum vitae Names and email addresses of at least three references Statement of teaching experience, effectiveness, and philosophy (no more than 2 pages) Statement of research goals (no more than 2 pages) Unofficial transcript Review of completed applications will commence on January 1, 2027; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Official graduate transcripts and successful completion of a background check is required upon hire. Questions may be sent via email to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Nathan Stansell at nstansell@niu.edu . Special Instructions Quick Link to Applicant https://employment.niu.edu/postings/97845 Is Background Check Required Yes EEO Statement Summary In accordance with applicable statutes and regulations, NIU is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, religion, age, disability (physical and mental), marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender (identity and expression), political affiliation, or any other factor unrelated to professional qualifications, and will comply with all applicable federal and state statutes, regulations and orders pertaining to nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Director of Civil Rights Office, Title IX Coordinator Health Services 2nd floor CivilRights@niu.edu 815-753-0455 Visa Policy In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification document form upon hire. ADA Accommodation NIU remains committed to ensuring that its recruitment and application procedures include full opportunities for applicants with disabilities. Employment opportunities will not be denied to anyone because of the need to make accommodations for a person’s disability during either the application or interview process. An applicant who believes they require an accommodation to participate in the employment process due to a disability may request that accommodation through the Accommodation Request Form . For further assistance, please contact the office of Affirmative Action and Equal Opportunity ( AAEO ) at ada@niu.edu . Safety Information NIU provides annual reports on campus security and fire safety. Read the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Contact the Ethics and Compliance Office at 815-753-9364 for a hard copy. Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae List of at least 3 Professional References Teaching Statement Research Statement Transcripts (unofficial with official required at hire) Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © 2019 Board of Trustees of Northern Illinois University All rights reserved. Back to Top Northern Illinois University 1425 W. Lincoln Hwy., DeKalb, IL 60115 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
